+<h2 id="taur-ahe">Taur-ahe Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="taur-ahe/grammar.md">taur-ahe/grammar.md</a>.
+Key patterns used: Apostrophe compounding (An'she, Mu'sha, Apa'ro);
+celestial deity names; <em>-ahe</em> as language/speech suffix.
+Taur-ahe is extremely poorly attested — no verb forms, particles, or
+sentence structures are known. All constructions below juxtapose attested
+morphemes or combine them with minimal assumptions.</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>T1</td>
+  <td>An'she, Mu'sha.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈɑnʃɛ ˈmuʃɑ/</td>
+  <td>Sun, Moon. (A greeting invoking both deities.)</td>
+  <td>Juxtaposition of two attested deity names; <strong>speculative</strong> — assumes invocation pattern</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>T2</td>
+  <td>Taur-ahe, An'she.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈtɑʊrɑhɛ ˈɑnʃɛ/</td>
+  <td>Earth-speech, Sun. (Earth speaks to the Sun.)</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Taur-ahe</em> (earth-speech/language) + attested <em>An'she</em> (sun); <strong>speculative</strong> — assumes <em>Taur-ahe</em> can function as a subject</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>T3</td>
+  <td>Apa'ro, Lo'sho.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈɑpɑroʊ ˈloʃoʊ/</td>
+  <td>White Stag, Earth. (An invocation of Malorne and the earth.)</td>
+  <td>Attested <em>Apa'ro</em> (white stag/Malorne) + attested <em>Lo'sho</em> (earth term); <strong>speculative</strong> juxtaposition</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
