+<!-- ============================================================ -->
+<h2 id="tolvir">Tol'vir Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="tolvir/grammar.md">tolvir/grammar.md</a>.
+Key patterns used: Drill-command imperatives (*Kadesh*, *Osadi*, *Satekh*);
+*Vir'-* water/river prefix; *Al'-* definite article; *-et* / *-ep* locative suffixes;
+hieroglyphic writing system. Tol'vir syntax is entirely unknown — only one untranslated
+sentence exists. All constructions below combine attested morphemes with minimal assumptions.</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Tv1</td>
+  <td>Kadesh! Osadi! Satekh!</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/kɑˈdɛʃ oˈsɑdi sɑˈtɛk/</td>
+  <td>Swing! Strike! Block!</td>
+  <td>Attested drill commands; combat training sequence</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Tv2</td>
+  <td>Vir'naal, khopesh.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/vɪrˈnɑl xoˈpɛʃ/</td>
+  <td>River-water, sickle-sword.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Vir'naal* (river system) + attested *khopesh* (sickle sword); <strong>speculative</strong> — juxtaposition of two confirmed nouns</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Tv3</td>
+  <td>Al'burq, Alra'ed.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ɑlˈburk ɑlˈrɑːɛd/</td>
+  <td>The lightning, the thunder.</td>
+  <td>Attested weapon names *Al'burq* + *Alra'ed*; if *Al'-* = definite article, these read as noun phrases</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Tv4</td>
+  <td>Nefer-set, Ramkahen.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/nɛˈfɜrsɛt rɑmˈkɑhɛn/</td>
+  <td>Beautiful-place, Ramkahen-settlement.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Neferset* (decomposed as *Nefer* + *-set*) + attested *Ramkahen*; <strong>highly speculative</strong> — assumes *Nefer* = "beautiful/good" and *-set* is locative</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Tv5</td>
+  <td>Murkash, Satekh!</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/murˈkɑʃ sɑˈtɛk/</td>
+  <td>[Battle cry], block!</td>
+  <td>Attested *Murkash!* (General Husam's cry) + attested *Satekh* (block command); <strong>speculative</strong> — assumes *Murkash* is a combat exclamation</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Tv6</td>
+  <td>Vir'sar, Ama-thet.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/vɪrˈsɑr ɑˈmɑθɛt/</td>
+  <td>Water-oasis, Sun-place.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Vir'sar* (oasis, decomposed *Vir* + *sar*) + speculative decomposition of *Amathet* as *Ama* + *-thet*; <strong>highly speculative</strong> — *Ama* meaning unknown</td>
+</tr>
+</table>
+
+<!-- ============================================================ -->
+<h2 id="drust">Drust Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="drust/grammar.md">drust/grammar.md</a>.
