+<h2 id="nerubian">Nerubian Constructed Sentences</h2>
+
+<p>Based on the grammar in <a href="nerubian/grammar.md">nerubian/grammar.md</a>.
+Key patterns used: *Anub-* lord/warrior prefix; *Azj-* deep/realm prefix; *-kahet*
+kingdom/realm suffix; apostrophe as morpheme boundary; right-headed compounding.
+Nerubian has <strong>no attested sentences or phrases at all</strong> — the entire corpus
+consists of proper names and place names. All constructions below are compound
+juxtapositions using inferred morphemes.</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>#</th><th>Sentence</th><th>IPA</th><th>Gloss</th><th>Grammar Used</th></tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Nr1</td>
+  <td>Anub'azal, Azj-Kahet.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ɑˈnʊbɑːˈzɑːl æzˈkɑːhɛt/</td>
+  <td>Lord-Azal, Deep-Kingdom.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Anub'azal* (the General) + attested *Azj-Kahet* (nerubian kingdom); juxtaposition of a military leader's title-name and his realm</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Nr2</td>
+  <td>Arak'nai, Azjol-Nerub.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ɑˈrɑːknaɪ ˈæzjoʊlˈnɛrʊb/</td>
+  <td>Weaver-[nai], [Azjol]-Nerub.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Arak'nai* (the Weaver) + attested *Azjol-Nerub* (Northrend kingdom); juxtaposition of a spymaster's title-name and the ancient nerubian realm</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Nr3</td>
+  <td>Anub'rek, Anub'arak.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ɑˈnʊbˈrɛk ɑˈnʊbəˈræk/</td>
+  <td>Lord-Rek, Lord-Arak.</td>
+  <td>Coined *Anub'rek* (*Anub-* + *-rek* suffix) + attested *Anub'arak* (King of Azjol-Nerub); <strong>speculative</strong> — assumes *Anub-* can productively combine with *-rek* suffix</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Nr4</td>
+  <td>Nerub-ar, Ahn'kahet.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈnɛrʊbɑːr ˈɑːnkɑːhɛt/</td>
+  <td>Nerub-realm, Old-Kingdom.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Nerub-ar* (Palace) + attested *Ahn'kahet* (the Old Kingdom); juxtaposition of two nerubian place names sharing the *-kahet* / *-ar* suffix pattern</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Nr5</td>
+  <td>Ovi'nax, Krix'vizk.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/ˈoʊvɪnæks ˈkrɪksvɪzk/</td>
+  <td>[Ovi]-brood, [Krix]-[vizk].</td>
+  <td>Attested *Ovi'nax* + attested *Krix'vizk*; juxtaposition of two TWW nerubian names showing the apostrophe compounding pattern</td>
+</tr>
+
+<tr class="non-canon">
+  <td>Nr6</td>
+  <td>Azj-kahet, Nazj-atar.</td>
+  <td class="ipa">/æzˈkɑːhɛt ˈnɔːzdʒətɑːr/</td>
+  <td>Deep-kingdom, N-Deep-domain.</td>
+  <td>Attested *Azj-Kahet* (nerubian) + attested *Nazjatar* (naga); if *Nazj-* = *N-* + *Azj-*, this juxtaposition demonstrates the shared Aqir substrate morpheme; <strong>highly speculative</strong> — the *Azj-*/*Nazj-* connection is unconfirmed</td>
