+<h2 id="arathi-dar">The -dar Suffix: Earthen or Arathi?</h2>
+
+<div class="note">
+<strong>Assessment:</strong> The <em>-dar</em> suffix in <em>Beledar</em> and <em>Mereldar</em>
+most likely derives from Titan <em>-dor</em> (land/realm) via Earthen. The suffix appears
+<strong>only</strong> in Khaz Algar — not in any other Arathi or Common place names — which
+strongly suggests an Earthen source (substrate or contact borrowing) rather than independent
+Arathi innovation. <strong>Confidence: Low&ndash;Medium.</strong>
+</div>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>Form</th><th>Language</th><th>Context</th><th>Sound Change</th></tr>
+<tr><td><em>-dor</em></td><td>Titan</td><td><em>Kalimdor</em> = "Land of Eternal Starlight"</td><td>Original</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>-dar</em></td><td>Earthen</td><td><em>Beledar</em>, <em>Mereldar</em> (Hallowfall)</td><td>Vowel raising: /ɔ/ &rarr; /ɑ/</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>Dorn-</em></td><td>Earthen</td><td><em>Dorn</em> (Isle of Dorn), <em>Dornogal</em></td><td>+ final /n/ (definiteness marker?)</td></tr>
+<tr><td><em>-modan</em></td><td>Dwarven</td><td><em>Khaz Modan</em></td><td>Further development (if *-modan* = *-dor* + *-an*)</td></tr>
+</table>
+
+<h2 id="arathi-names">Arathi Personal Names (Hallowfall)</h2>
+
+<p>The Arathi of Hallowfall are a mixed human&ndash;high-elf population. Their personal names reflect
+this dual heritage, though the sample is too small for morphological analysis.</p>
+
+<table>
+<tr><th>Name</th><th>IPA</th><th>Role</th><th>Linguistic Affiliation</th></tr>
+<tr><td>Faerin Lothar</td><td class="ipa">/ˈfɛərɪn/</td><td>Arathi Lamplighter</td><td>Common/Human; "Lothar" is the Arathi dynasty; "Faerin" may have Elven influence</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Vaelisia Steelstrike</td><td class="ipa">/vɛˈliːsiə/</td><td>General of Arathi military</td><td>Mixed; given name has Elven phonological features; surname is English compound</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Aelric Leid</td><td class="ipa">/ˈɛlrɪk/</td><td>Order of Night leader (void cultist)</td><td>Common/Germanic; "Ælfric" pattern</td></tr>
+</table>
+
+<p>The primary linguistic significance of the Arathi data is the <em>-dar</em> toponymic suffix
+in place names (*Beledar*, *Mereldar*), which connects to the Earthen/Titan *-dor* morpheme
+and suggests that the Arathi adopted Earthen place names when they settled in Hallowfall.</p>
+
