<h1>Alien Languages of Azeroth</h1>

<p>A comparative analysis of the four "alien" languages of World of Warcraft:
<a href="shath-yar/description.md">Shath'Yar</a> (Old Gods and their servants),
<a href="nerubian/description.md">Nerubian</a> (spider-people of Azj-Kahet),
<a href="qiraji/description.md">Qiraji</a> (insectoid servants of C'Thun in Silithus), and
<a href="ethereal/description.md">Ethereal / Broker</a> (energy beings from K'aresh).
These languages share no confirmed genetic relationship to the elven or titan-forged
language families, but exhibit striking parallels in orthographic conventions (especially
apostrophe-marked morpheme boundaries) and, in the case of nerubian and qiraji, a potential
shared Aqir substrate.</p>

<div class="note">
<strong>Methodological caveat:</strong> The attested corpus for all four languages is extremely small.
None has any attested sentences &mdash; the entire corpus for each consists of proper names and place names.
Shath'Yar has a few opaque phrases without translations. All morpheme decompositions and
reconstructed forms are provisional. Forms marked <span class="inferred">in purple</span> are inferred;
forms marked <span class="uncertain">in gray italics</span> have uncertain glosses. Confidence ratings:
<span class="confidence-high">High</span>,
<span class="confidence-mod">Low&ndash;Moderate</span>,
<span class="confidence-low">Very Low</span>.
</div>

