+<h3>Kobyss: Linguistic Regression</h3>
+
 <div class="note">
-<strong>Confidence: Very Low</strong> for kobyss-language analysis (no data);
-<strong>Moderate</strong> for ankoan descent classification (wiki-confirmed lore).
+<strong>Critical finding:</strong> Kobyss "are capable of speech but only use simple phrases like
+'Animate bones', 'Devour', and 'Violence'" (warcraft.wiki.gg). These are <strong>Common-language
+utterances</strong>, not kobyss-language words. This suggests near-total loss of the ankoan/jinyu language
+— a reversal of the murloc→jinyu evolution. Where the Vale of Eternal Blossoms <em>expanded</em> jinyu
+minds and language, the Undersea and Void energy appear to have <em>contracted</em> kobyss minds and language.
 </div>
 
