 <table>
-<tr><th>Stele</th><th>Summary</th><th>Location</th></tr>
-<tr><td>Drust Stele: Conflict</td><td>Shows multiple conflicts: Drust fighting themselves, gnomes, naga, and finally humans with anchor sigils</td><td>Crimson Forest</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Drust Stele: The Tree</td><td>Shows a massive tree surrounded by worshipful Drust</td><td>Crimson Forest</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Drust Stele: The Circle</td><td>Depicts a group of Drust</td><td>Gol Osigr area</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Drust Stele: The Ritual</td><td>(Full text not yet recovered)</td><td>Iceveil Glacier</td></tr>
-<tr><td>Drust Stele: Protectors of the Forest</td><td>(Full text not yet recovered)</td><td>Ulfar's Den area</td></tr>
+<tr><th>Stele</th><th>Full Inscription Text</th><th>Location</th></tr>
+<tr><td>Drust Stele: Conflict</td><td>&lt;This stone shows multiple conflicts or one great battle with many scenes. In the oldest they fight beings that look like themselves or great beasts. In others they fight much smaller beings that resemble gnomes in stature. In another the Drust are driving some Naga back into the seas. Where the carving is most recent the Drust are fighting men and women bearing anchor sigils.&gt;</td><td>Crimson Forest</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Drust Stele: The Tree</td><td>&lt;The carving shows a massive tree, bigger than the others marked onto the stone. It is surrounded by worshipful Drust.&gt;</td><td>Crimson Forest</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Drust Stele: The Circle</td><td>&lt;The weathered cairn depicts a group of Drust...&gt;</td><td>Gol Osigr area</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Drust Stele: Constructs</td><td>&lt;There are many scenes on this stone but three are clear. The Drust are building large, person-shaped constructs in one image. In a second, a person is killed over the chest of one construct. In a third the stone creature walks into battle, taller than even the Drust.&gt;</td><td>Drustvar</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Drust Stele: The Ritual</td><td>&lt;The Drust carved onto this stone appears to carry a curved blade in one hand. The head of a man or animal is in his other hand. At his feet are the bodies of many slain animals. Their entrails are being observed by other Drust.&gt;</td><td>Iceveil Glacier</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Drust Stele: Breath Into Stone</td><td>&lt;The carving looks like breath or wind is being drawn from a body and put into a stone.&gt;</td><td>Gol Koval area</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Drust Stele: Sacrifice</td><td>&lt;The weathered stone has a worn groove across the middle, as if a blade has struck down the same line over centuries. Dark stains mark one side of the worn cut.&gt;</td><td>Drustvar</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Drust Stele: The Cycle</td><td>&lt;This image shows a single tree in multiple states of life. On the right the leaves are small and low to the ground like a sapling. In the center of the tree the branches are tall and strong, the leaves large and open. On the left the branches are thin, broken and mostly bare. The last vestiges of dried red-black pigment cling to the ancient stone to mark fallen leaves. A stylized sun passes over the tree.&gt;</td><td>Drustvar</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Drust Stele: The Flayed Man</td><td>&lt;The carving on this stone is of a life-sized Drust who has been flayed. The placement of important organs is surprisingly accurate despite the stylization and primitive materials. The eyes are white stones with the faint remains of paint on them. They seem to follow you around. At one point there were prayers, or instructions, carved around the body, but time has rendered the runes illegible. The carving was done with great care, but the purpose remains unknown.&gt;</td><td>Drustvar</td></tr>
+<tr><td>Drust Stele: Protectors of the Forest</td><td>&lt;A great bramblebear, possibly a Drust druid, is posed with their head bowed to a massive stag and doe. The deer appear to be blessing the bear or accepting its supplication. The stag's coat was once whitewashed while the doe's was covered with blackened soot.&gt;</td><td>Ulfar's Den area</td></tr>
 </table>
 
+<div class="note">
+<strong>Note:</strong> There is no stele titled "The Three." The achievement "Drust the Facts, Ma'am" lists exactly 10 steles: Conflict, The Tree, The Circle, The Ritual, Breath Into Stone, Sacrifice, Constructs, The Cycle, The Flayed Man, Protectors of the Forest. All 10 inscription texts have been recovered from warcraft.wiki.gg.
+</div>
+
